+Please integrate the visual bubble tracking from rep-tracker.tsx with the dynamic calculation logic in double-pyramid.tsx.
+
+Step 1: Update RepTracker
+Modify src/app/components/rep-tracker.tsx so that repSequence is no longer a hardcoded constant. Instead, it should accept repSequence as a prop ({ repSequence }: { repSequence: number[] }).
+
+Add a check: if repSequence is empty or undefined, display a fallback message or return null.
+
+Keep all the visual bubble logic, the currentIndex state, and the Next/Previous/Reset button functionality exactly as it is.
+
+Step 2: Update DoublePyramid
+Modify src/app/components/double-pyramid.tsx to import and render the updated <RepTracker /> component.
+
+Place the <RepTracker /> component directly between the "Pyramid Configuration" block and the "Set Tracking" block.
+
+Create a derived variable that maps the current sets state into an array of numbers (e.g., const currentSequence = sets.map(s => parseInt(s.reps) || 0);).
+
+Pass currentSequence as the repSequence prop to the <RepTracker />.
+
+Step 3: Reset functionality
+When the user clicks "Generate Pyramid Sets" or "Clear Pyramid" in the DoublePyramid component, it needs to force the RepTracker to reset its currentIndex back to 0. You can achieve this by passing a key prop to <RepTracker /> based on the sets length or a state trigger, or by lifting the currentIndex state up into DoublePyramid. Choose the cleanest React approach.

